            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Every piece traced to a root:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "je from ego (English ego)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "me from mē (English me, my, mine)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "(s')appeler from appellāre (English appeal, appellation)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "comment from quo modo (Spanish cómo, English mode)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "enchanté from in-cantāre (English enchant, incantation, chant)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And two habits of French to keep: it gives a name with a reflexive verb (\"I call myself\") and asks for one with \"how\" (\"how are you called?\"), and it makes politeness by using the plural vous on one person."
            }
